From 705ec793a7d785e27b090188a3a0d7a8c162a9e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:24:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor: zero CLU11 TX (factory cruise MAIN
 lockout) + pause/resume re-engage, no auto-resume

Root cause of the pedal FAULT_SCE onsets on routes 11c/123: our CLU11 (0x4F1) CANCEL frames collide with the
cluster's own CLU11 on bus 0. The panda can't intercept the buttons (cluster, ECM and panda share bus 0), so the
factory cruise is locked out instead: it can only engage while its MAIN is armed (EMS16 CRUISE_LAMP_M), and
pedal-long now refuses to run while MAIN is armed (car: nonAdaptive -> wrongCruiseMode; panda:
hyundai_factory_main_on clears controls and blocks every grant). openpilot sends ZERO CLU11 in this mode (removed
from the car controller and from the panda TX allowlist).

Pause/resume (CF_Clu_CruiseSwState 4): disengages while engaged (as before). While disengaged, a deliberate press
re-engages via resumeCruise (v_cruise restored by VCruiseHelper.initialize_v_cruise), only if brake and gas were
released for the whole press and the 60 ms release debounce. Panda mirrors it sample for sample. SET/RES pressed
with the brake down (incl. held across the brake release) can't engage. No auto-resume: nothing but a driver
button edge grants controls_allowed or buttonEnable.
